{"schemaVersion":1,"framework":"react","version":"v4","id":"errors/resource-render","title":"ResourceRenderError","description":"When ResourceRenderError occurs and how to resolve it.","body":[{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["A resource render-state boundary catches an exception while rendering a named state. It wraps the original exception unless it is already a ResourceModuleLoadError or ResourceRenderError."]},"\n",{"tag":"mdx:h2","props":{"id":"identify-the-error"},"children":["Identify the error"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":[["The error code is ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["resourceRender"]},". This class extends native ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["Error"]},", independently of ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["ReactLayoutError"]},"."]]},"\n",{"tag":"mdx:h2","props":{"id":"separate-resource-and-lazy-fallbacks"},"children":["Separate resource and lazy fallbacks"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":[["A resource render-state boundary can wrap render exceptions. A lazy ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["Error"]}," fallback handles loading, module shape, and missing lazy state failures only; it does not catch arbitrary render exceptions. Use an outer React error boundary for those exceptions."]]},"\n",{"tag":"mdx:h2","props":{"id":"resolve-the-error"},"children":["Resolve the error"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["Inspect resource, state and cause, then correct the failing render logic. A configured resource Error state can receive this wrapper."]},"\n",{"tag":"mdx:h2","props":{"id":"release-scope"},"children":["Release scope"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":[["This page describes ",{"tag":"code","props":{},"children":["@jfdevelops/react-layout@4.1.0"]},". The behavior is based on the error definitions and their call sites in ",{"tag":"mdx:a","props":{"href":"https://github.com/jfdevelops/react-layout/blob/%40jfdevelops%2Freact-layout%404.1.0/packages/core/src/errors/resource-state-error.ts"},"children":["the tagged source"]},"."]]},"\n",{"tag":"mdx:h2","props":{"id":"next-steps"},"children":["Next steps"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","props":{},"children":[["\n",{"tag":"li","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"mdx:a","props":{"href":"../guides/troubleshooting.md"},"children":["Troubleshooting"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"mdx:a","props":{"href":"../standard-schema.md"},"children":["Standard Schema"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"mdx:a","props":{"href":"../reference/index.md"},"children":["API reference"]}]},"\n"]]}],"toc":[{"title":"Identify the error","url":"#identify-the-error","depth":2},{"title":"Separate resource and lazy fallbacks","url":"#separate-resource-and-lazy-fallbacks","depth":2},{"title":"Resolve the error","url":"#resolve-the-error","depth":2},{"title":"Release scope","url":"#release-scope","depth":2},{"title":"Next steps","url":"#next-steps","depth":2}]}